2, "prompt": "A disorder in which nerve cell activity in the brain is disturbed, causing seizures.\nAsnwer _____________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1798, "answer": {"text": ":D", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 8, "prompt": "What is the common reason for Battens Disease?\nAnswer ______________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 539, "answer": {"text": "mutation of the CLN2 gene", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "Which can transduce postmitotic cells?\nAnswer_______________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 612, "answer": {"text": "Adeno-associated viruses", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "Which is a known complication of late LINCL?\nAnswer_______________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 677, "answer": {"text": "epilepticus", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "What are the two conditions which are known to arise not out of therapy ?\nAnswer_____________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 749, "answer": {"text": ": vomiting and thrombocytosis", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "What is used to maximize the enzyme dispensation through cross-correction?\nAnswer______________", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "mannose-6-phosphate pathway", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 13, "prompt": "Which is the effective long-term therapy in LINCL?\nAnswer_______________", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 101, "answer": {"text": "Gene therapy", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "What dosage of the AAV2Hcln2 vector did the participants receive?\nAnswer_______________", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 179, "answer": {"text": "2.5 Ã— 1012 particles", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 16, "prompt": ". The ____________ gene provides instructions for making an enzyme called\ntripeptidyl peptidase 1.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 515, "answer": {"text": ": Tpp1", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 17, "prompt": "It is always not required to introduce ____________ to CNS.\n18.____________ made it all clear that the therapy can have more positive impact\non the disease.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 618, "answer": {"text": "Cln2 Cdna", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "Out of all the mutations, _____________ are considered to be the major causes\nfor the disease to appear in infants and adults.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 781, "answer": {"text": "Three", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": ".The______________ gene provides instructions for making a protein whose\nfunction is not well understood", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 913, "answer": {"text": ":Cln6", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "00e085f1f6ddd317-p6", "label": "Part B · PART B", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "00e085f1f6ddd317cd05051992da1ba59a1fa0f33049f080f3339557e0b6b227", "pages": [6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11], "questions": [{"number": 1, "prompt": ".What does the notice indicates?\nAngina pectoris is common among people.\nThere is a direct relationship between the functioning of liver and Qi blood of\nthe heart.\nVarious ailments can lead to angina pectoris.\nAngina pectoris\nAngina pectoris, whose common type is Qi-blood stagnation type is one of chest\ncongestion in TCM. The main cause of this type of angina is damage due to an\nexcess of seven emotions. The heart governs the mind and blood circulation, liver\nstores of blood and controls catharsis. There is close relationship between the two.\nOnly if liver function is normal can Qi-blood of the heart can be calm. For elderly\nindividuals, who lack Qi-blood, yin and yang of the heart, spleen and kidney, are\nof cold invasion, consume an inappropriate diet, have emotional disorders and\nexcessive fatigue, among others, can also lead to blood stasis stagnation, which can\nconsequently cause coronary angina pectoris of Qi-blood stagnation. The\n‘Suwen•Yujizhenzang’ theory has described “blockage of vessel, inability of QI to\nflow freely”, which illustrates that blood stagnation can lead to Qi depression.\nTherefore, accelerating blood circulation, removing blood stasis and promoting the\ncirculation of Qi are the main therapies.", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 210, "answer": {"text": "Various ailments can lead to angina pectoris.", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 4, "prompt": ".What is correct about metabonomics?\nHigh-throughput metabolomic approach revealed the acupuncture exerting\nintervention effects.\nMetabolomics has seen a surge in popularity in recent scientific research.\nThe ultimate aim of metabonomics is to detect every small-molecule\nmetabolite.\nMetabonomics\nMetabonomics as an advanced technology of systems biology has made\nconsiderable contributions to early diagnosis of serious illness, toxicology and\npharmacology. Early, accurate diagnosis of tumours, such as liver cancer and\novarian cancer, is a distinguishing feature and advantage of metabonomics. Valine,\nsaturated lipids, glycine, lactate, inositol, nucleotides, polyunsaturated fatty acids,\ntaurine and other tumour-related metabolic markers can be identified by\nmetabolomics, which makes metabonomics increasingly applicable to diagnosis,\ntherapy and prognostic evaluation. Acupuncture has a therapeutic effect for\ntumours: it can improve symptoms, prolong the lifespan of patients, improve the\nquality of life, relieve cancer pain syndrome and, especially, improve the side\neffects of radiotherapy and chemotherapy, eg, myelosuppression, gastrointestinal\nreaction, fever etc. Acupuncture treatment of tumour possesses many features and\nadvantages. Applying metabonomics to research investigating acupuncture\ntreatment of tumours both gives play to the sensitive detection advantage of\nmetabonomics for tumour diagnosis, treatment assessment and exploring the\nmechanism of acupuncture treatment at deeper, more extensive and more dynamic\nlevels. In addition, there are some reports investigating Alzheimer diseases at home\nand abroad, however, few in research of venereal disease.", "sourcePage": 9, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "Metabolomics has seen a surge in popularity in recent scientific research.", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": ".What does this notice indicate?\nThe curative effect of improving disease condition in treatment group is\nsuperior to the control group.\ntwo groups differ only by minor values.\ntotal effectiveness of the control group is lesser than treatment group.\nTreatment Groups - Recent Analysis\nTotal effective\nGroups         Cases     excellent     effective   Ineffective    exacerbated\nrate, %\nControl        40        19            9           10             2                 70.0\nTreatment      41        28            9           4              0                 90.2*", "sourcePage": 10, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "The curative effect of improving disease condition in treatment group is superior", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 6, "prompt": ".What does the result indicate?\nThe results indicate that subjects in the two groups improved after treatment.\nThe laboratory indexes of the treatment group significantly declined.\nAfter treatment, the laboratory indexes of the observation group were also\nmore declined than the control group.\nDisease Treatment Results - Before and After\nControl group (n=58)                 Observation group (n=59)\nBefore            After              Before              After\nIndex                        treatment         treatment          treatment           treatment\nFBG, mmol/L                  9.85 ± 1.25       8.53 ± 1.42        9.92 ± 1.25         7.21 ± 1.33*\nPBG, mmol/L                  13.54 ± 2.73      11.32 ± 2.89       14.07 ± 2.32        9.25 ± 1.08*\nHbA1c, %                     11.02 ± 2.34      10.32 ± 2.53       11.31 ± 1.97        8.79 ± 1.17*\nMicroalbuminuria, mg/L       81.24 ± 11.93     76.42 ± 12.33*     82.31 ± 10.64       45.22 ± 13.17*", "sourcePage": 11, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "The results indicate that subjects in the two groups improved after treatment.", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "00e085f1f6ddd317-p12", "label": "Part C · READING 23.pdf", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "00e085f1f6ddd317cd05051992da1ba59a1fa0f33049f080f3339557e0b6b227", "pages": [12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20], "questions": [{"number": 9, "prompt": "According to the passage, symptoms of Addisonâ€™s disease occur;\nSlowly\nSuddenly\nAfter a month\nSlowly after many months", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 750, "answer": {"text": "Slowly after many months", "source": {"id": "offline-837890d83f9943bd30b5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 23.pdf", "sha256": "837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/837890d83f9943bd30b541ea9284c304f715b05de4070947a726e370b2a72ae8.pdf", "textPath":